 "use_for": "Four-operator FM keys, bells and basses with eight algorithms.",
 "quirks": [
  "MIDI notes (notes_write's default) take any of its voices up to Voices (8 by default, 16 at most), a free one first, else the one released longest ago; a note's velocity does what the Velocity column does, for that note (velocity / 127, through each operator's VelSens); pitch bend moves every voice ±2 semitones, the mod wheel brings in the LFO's vibrato (as LFO Pitch, up to its maximum) and the sustain pedal holds released notes.",
  "Its Note track (notes_write with input \"tracks\") still plays as before, for old songs: one voice per track (16 at most; Voices caps it), and velocity is the per-track Velocity column (sticky: it holds for later notes).",
  "Glide only slides between overlapping notes on the same voice (a held MIDI key's voice, or a track).",
  "The profiler heard A2 for every note on its default patch: a bright FM spectrum fools the pitch tracker. Its source plays 440 · 2^((note − 69)/12) times each operator's ratio, the note conversion Pedal SH101 uses (measured at 440 Hz), so notes play as written.",
  "Operators run in order 1 → 4; which ones are heard (carriers) depends on Algorithm: in 1 (linear chain) only Operator 4.",
  "Every parameter at its maximum at once peaks above 0 dBFS (+4.1 dBFS over 30 s); no single parameter does."
 ],
